# Public download — it has to work

When this repo is public, a stranger must be able to clone or install Joblio and run it **on one PC with no office network, Docker, ngrok, or API key**.

## Default path (public / single PC)

- First-run **Start on this computer** → `jobs.db` under this PC’s app data
- Proofs live next to that file (`proofs\`)
- SQLite is the default. Self-host Docker is optional and documented in `self-host/`
- Auto-update against `\\server\...` must **quietly skip** if that share does not exist
- Shop PCs that **can** see `\\server\...` must still find `joblio-api-key.txt`, proofs, and updates **without** re-running Setup (see `shop-compat.mdc`)
- Public installers live on **GitHub Releases** (`https://github.com/MitchellPel/Joblio/releases/latest`). Shop PCs still update from the office share. A version bump must hit **both**.
- Self-host LAN / ngrok URLs and AI keys live in env, Settings, or a **reachable** share file — never bake a live tunnel hostname as the only URL. Keep office UNC **probes** in `electron/utils/officeShare.ts`

## Team path (office)

- Setup still offers **shared folder** so shop PCs can use one `jobs.db`
- Do not remove or break that flow

## Do not

- Hardcode office UNC paths, LAN IPs, or ngrok URLs as the only way to start
- Require `joblio-api-key.txt` for local SQLite
- Put secrets, `jobs.db`, or `Reference Program/` (AGPL) in git
- Assume every installer is updated from the office share
